/-!
# Odd orthogonal FF parameter restrictions

The imported reductions construct a faithful offender supplement with
quasisimple generalized Fitting subgroup and the original simple quotient.
They also construct its absolutely irreducible endomorphism-field action,
retaining the same elementary offender and its exact cardinality inequality.

The numerical restrictions remain open: split orthogonal groups must be
excluded, while odd rank at least two and minus rank at least two must
reduce to rank two over the field of order three. The low-rank comparisons,
large-rank degree bounds and exceptional Ω₇(3) estimate remain necessary.
No parameter restriction is asserted by the reductions alone.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith B.1.13, printed pp.73--74; Guralnick--Malle I,
Proposition 4.5, and II, Table 2. See `OrthogonalParameters/Source.md`.
-/
